msgid "Update"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"It is with great pleasure that we are announcing the release of Quarkus 3.7."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"With Quarkus 3.7, we begin the journey that will lead to Quarkus 3.8 being "
"the next LTS version of Quarkus.\n"
"We strongly encourage you to update to this version and provide feedback to "
"make our next LTS version strong and stable."
msgstr ""

msgid "Major changes are:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/pull/37335[#37335] - Java 17 is the new "
"baseline"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/pull/38190[#38190] - Rename RESTEasy "
"Classic client extensions to resteasy-client"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/pull/36978[#36978] - Upgrade to "
"Hibernate ORM 6.4, Hibernate Search 7.0, Hibernate Reactive 2.2"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/pull/35065[#35065] - Add Hibernate "
"Search management endpoint"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/pull/36945[#36945] - Support Micrometer "
"`@MeterTag`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/pull/37152[#37152] - Support token "
"verification with the inlined certificate chain"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/pull/37269[#37269] - Support "
"certificate role mappings"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/pull/37472[#37472] - Provide a way to "
"observe security events"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/pull/37730[#37730] - Introduce LinkedIn "
"OIDC provider"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/pull/37891[#37891] - Split OIDC session "
"cookie if its size is more than 4KB"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/pull/38029[#38029] - Allow applications "
"using quakus-info to contribute data to the /info using CDI"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/pull/38066[#38066] - Drop Okhttp/Okio "
"from BOM"
msgstr ""

msgid "3.7.1 also fixes the following CVEs:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2023-5675[CVE-2023-5675] "
"Authorization flaw in Quarkus RESTEasy Reactive and Classic when `quarkus."
"security.jaxrs.deny-unannotated-endpoints` or `quarkus.security.jaxrs."
"default-roles-allowed` properties are used"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2023-6267[CVE-2023-6267] JSON "
"payload getting processed prior to security checks when REST resources are "
"used with annotations"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We also released 3.6.9 to address these issues in 3.6, in case you encounter "
"problems updating to 3.7."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"As usual, this version also comes with bugfixes, performance improvements "
"and documentation improvements."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"As mentioned in the previous minor announcement, we currently maintain two "
"version streams in the community:"
msgstr ""

msgid "3.7: it is the latest and greatest and it introduces new features"
msgstr ""

msgid "3.2: it is our current link:/blog/lts-releases/[LTS release]"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus 2.x is not maintained in the community anymore.\n"
"If you are using the community version, please upgrade to Quarkus 3.x "
"(either 3.2 LTS or 3.7).\n"
"We recommend using `quarkus update` to do so."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To update to Quarkus 3.7, we recommend updating to the latest version of the "
"Quarkus CLI and run:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Note that `quarkus update` can update your applications from any version of "
"Quarkus (including 2.x) to Quarkus 3.7."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To migrate from 3.6, please refer to https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/"
"wiki/Migration-Guide-3.7[our migration guide]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you are not already using 3.x, please refer to the https://quarkus.io/"
"blog/quarkus-3-0-final-released/[3.0 announcement] for all the details.\n"
"You can also refer to https://quarkus.io/blog/quarkus-3-upgrade/[this blog "
"post] for additional details.\n"
"Once you upgraded to 3.0, also have a look at the https://github.com/"
"quarkusio/quarkus/wiki/Migration-Guide-3.1[3.1], https://github.com/"
"quarkusio/quarkus/wiki/Migration-Guide-3.2[3.2], https://github.com/"
"quarkusio/quarkus/wiki/Migration-Guide-3.3[3.3], https://github.com/"
"quarkusio/quarkus/wiki/Migration-Guide-3.4[3.4], https://github.com/"
"quarkusio/quarkus/wiki/Migration-Guide-3.5[3.5], and https://github.com/"
"quarkusio/quarkus/wiki/Migration-Guide-3.6[3.6] migration guides."
msgstr ""

msgid "What&#8217;s new?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Java 17 is the new baseline"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"As was announced at https://quarkus.io/blog/java-17/[the end of November], "
"you will need a Java 17+ runtime (using Java 21 is encouraged!) to run "
"Quarkus 3.7 applications."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When we released Quarkus 3.0, we announced that Java 11 support was "
"deprecated and would go away at some point.\n"
"This is the time."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Most of the Java ecosystem is moving to Java 17 as the baseline so it wasn't "
"sustainable for Quarkus to support Java 11 much longer."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If your Java 17 migration is ongoing, you can upgrade to the latest 3.6 but "
"keep in mind that 3.6.9 released today is the latest 3.6.\n"
"If you are stuck with Java 11 for some time, we recommend using Quarkus 3.2 "
"LTS as it will be maintained longer."
msgstr ""

msgid "RESTEasy Classic Client extensions renamed"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"As part of the renaming of the RESTEasy Reactive extensions that will be "
"spread across several releases, we renamed the `quarkus-rest-client*` "
"extensions (client extensions for RESTEasy Classic) to `quarkus-resteasy-"
"client*`, which makes it clearer that it is the client counterpart of "
"`quarkus-resteasy`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Relocations have been put in place to not break your applications but we "
"recommend that you adjust your applications already as these particular "
"artifacts (`quarkus-rest-client*`) will be switched to RESTEasy Reactive in "
"Quarkus 3.9."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"See https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/blob/main/adr/0002-reactive-rename."
"adoc for the full context of this change."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We encourage you to move to the new artifacts listed in the following table:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Old name"
msgstr ""

msgid "New name"
msgstr ""

msgid "quarkus-rest-client"
msgstr ""

msgid "quarkus-resteasy-client"
msgstr ""

msgid "quarkus-rest-client-jackson"
msgstr ""

msgid "quarkus-resteasy-client-jackson"
msgstr ""

msgid "quarkus-rest-client-jaxb"
msgstr ""

msgid "quarkus-resteasy-client-jaxb"
msgstr ""

msgid "quarkus-rest-client-jsonb"
msgstr ""

msgid "quarkus-resteasy-client-jsonb"
msgstr ""

msgid "quarkus-rest-client-mutiny"
msgstr ""

msgid "quarkus-resteasy-client-mutiny"
msgstr ""

msgid "Hibernate ORM 6.4, Hibernate Search 7.0, Hibernate Reactive 2.2"
msgstr ""

msgid "We updated the Hibernate persistence stack to:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Hibernate ORM 6.4 - see https://in.relation.to/2023/11/23/orm-640-final/"
"[announcement]"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Hibernate Search 7.0 - see https://in.relation.to/2023/12/05/hibernate-"
"search-7-0-0-Final/[announcement]"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Hibernate Reactive 2.2 - see https://in.relation.to/2023/11/28/hibernate-"
"reactive-2_2_Final/[announcement]"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We now expose a management endpoint for Hibernate Search, which allows to "
"trigger mass indexing and other maintenance tasks.\n"
"You can find out more about it in the https://quarkus.io/guides/hibernate-"
"search-orm-elasticsearch#management[updated documentation]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Micrometer @MeterTag"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Micrometer `@MeterTag` can now be used to dynamically assign tag values to "
"metrics.\n"
"See the https://quarkus.io/guides/telemetry-micrometer#annotations[dedicated "
"doc section] for more information."
msgstr ""

msgid "Assorted security improvements"
msgstr ""

msgid "Our security extensions got a bunch of new features, improvements:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Contribute data to /info endpoint"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"All CDI beans implementing `InfoContributor` will contribute to the `/info` "
"endpoint."
msgstr ""

msgid "Okhttp/Okio versions not enforced anymore"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"As we didn't want to rely on the Kotlin runtime for non-Kotlin-related "
"extensions,\n"
"we were enforcing a very old version of Okhttp in Quarkus,\n"
"thus making using newer Okhttp version harder."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For several versions, we have been working on reducing our dependency to "
"Okhttp\n"
"to be able to avoid enforcing the version in Quarkus."
msgstr ""

msgid "This is now effective in 3.7."
msgstr ""

msgid "Full changelog"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can get the full changelog of https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/"
"releases/tag/3.7.0.CR1[3.7.0.CR1], https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/"
"releases/tag/3.7.0[3.7.0], and https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/releases/"
"tag/3.7.1[3.7.1] on GitHub."
msgstr ""

